<Programs>
<Program Name="MainProgram" TestEdits="false" MainRoutineName="MainRoutine" Disabled="false" UseAsFolder="false">
<Tags/>
<Routines>
<Routine Name="AutoSeq_V5" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Start Auto Motion. One-shot latch off the HMI momentary pushbutton.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Start_Auto_PB)ONS(Start_ONS)OTL(Auto_Running)OTU(Servo_On_Timeout);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Stop. Drop auto and force the shutdown step. Shutdown rungs are NOT gated by Auto_Running.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Stop_PB)OTU(Auto_Running)MOVE(99,Seq_Step);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Idle to MSO. Step 0 rolls to step 1 as soon as auto is running.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Auto_Running)EQ(Seq_Step,0)MOVE(1,Seq_Step);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Step 1. MSO axes 141-145 on its own timer. Axis 146 is never commanded. 800 ms settle.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Auto_Running)EQ(Seq_Step,1)MSO(Zippy_Axis_141,MSO_141)MSO(Zippy_Axis_142,MSO_142)MSO(Zippy_Axis_143,MSO_143)MSO(Zippy_Axis_144,MSO_144)MSO(Zippy_Axis_145,MSO_145)MOVE(800,MSO_TMR.PRE)TON(MSO_TMR,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Servo-on proof. All five in ServoActionStatus, in series - every axis, not any axis. Computed every scan; only read at step 1.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Zippy_Axis_141.ServoActionStatus)XIC(Zippy_Axis_142.ServoActionStatus)XIC(Zippy_Axis_143.ServoActionStatus)XIC(Zippy_Axis_144.ServoActionStatus)XIC(Zippy_Axis_145.ServoActionStatus)OTE(All_Servos_On);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Servo-on timeout. The 800 ms settle expired and at least one axis never enabled. The sequence deliberately does NOT advance - it stops here and faults, because the alternative is jogging an axis that is not on. Latched so it survives the stop; rung 0 clears it on the next start attempt.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Auto_Running)EQ(Seq_Step,1)XIC(MSO_TMR.DN)XIO(All_Servos_On)OTL(Servo_On_Timeout);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Advance out of step 1 only with proof: the settle expired AND all five axes report servo action AND this start attempt has not already timed out. Seq_TMR.DN is still 0 here, so the next rung cannot double-advance.
The XIO(Servo_On_Timeout) makes a timeout a failed start rather than a slow one - once it latches, the only way forward is stop and start again. If a drive on this cell genuinely needs longer than 800 ms to enable, raise MSO_TMR.PRE in rung 3; do not delete this contact.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Auto_Running)EQ(Seq_Step,1)XIC(MSO_TMR.DN)XIC(All_Servos_On)XIO(Servo_On_Timeout)MOVE(2,Seq_Step);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Advance motion steps 2-11 on Seq_TMR.DN. RES restarts the timebase because the step timer rung stays true across all ten steps.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Auto_Running)GE(Seq_Step,2)LE(Seq_Step,11)XIC(Seq_TMR.DN)ADD(Seq_Step,1,Seq_Step)RES(Seq_TMR);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Wrap. Step 11 increments to 12, caught here and folded back to step 2 for a continuous loop.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Auto_Running)EQ(Seq_Step,12)ADD(Cycle_Count,1,Cycle_Count)MOVE(2,Seq_Step);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Step 2. Jog 141 forward.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Auto_Running)EQ(Seq_Step,2)MAJ(Zippy_Axis_141,MAJ_141,0,Jog_Speed,0,Jog_Accel,0,Jog_Decel,0,0,100.0,100.0,2,1,0,0.0,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Step 3. Stop 141, jog 142 forward.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Auto_Running)EQ(Seq_Step,3)MAS(Zippy_Axis_141,MAS_141,0,1,Jog_Decel,0,0,100.0,2)MAJ(Zippy_Axis_142,MAJ_142,0,Jog_Speed,0,Jog_Accel,0,Jog_Decel,0,0,100.0,100.0,2,1,0,0.0,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Step 4. Stop 142, jog 143 forward.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Auto_Running)EQ(Seq_Step,4)MAS(Zippy_Axis_142,MAS_142,0,1,Jog_Decel,0,0,100.0,2)MAJ(Zippy_Axis_143,MAJ_143,0,Jog_Speed,0,Jog_Accel,0,Jog_Decel,0,0,100.0,100.0,2,1,0,0.0,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Step 5. Stop 143, jog 144 forward.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Auto_Running)EQ(Seq_Step,5)MAS(Zippy_Axis_143,MAS_143,0,1,Jog_Decel,0,0,100.0,2)MAJ(Zippy_Axis_144,MAJ_144,0,Jog_Speed,0,Jog_Accel,0,Jog_Decel,0,0,100.0,100.0,2,1,0,0.0,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Step 6. Stop 144, jog 145 forward. Far end of the run.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Auto_Running)EQ(Seq_Step,6)MAS(Zippy_Axis_144,MAS_144,0,1,Jog_Decel,0,0,100.0,2)MAJ(Zippy_Axis_145,MAJ_145,0,Jog_Speed,0,Jog_Accel,0,Jog_Decel,0,0,100.0,100.0,2,1,0,0.0,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="14" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Step 7. Reverse 145. Merge is enabled on the MAJ so it replaces the forward jog on that axis.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Auto_Running)EQ(Seq_Step,7)MAJ(Zippy_Axis_145,MAJ_145,1,Jog_Speed,0,Jog_Accel,0,Jog_Decel,0,0,100.0,100.0,2,1,0,0.0,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="15" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Step 8. Stop 145, reverse 144.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Auto_Running)EQ(Seq_Step,8)MAS(Zippy_Axis_145,MAS_145,0,1,Jog_Decel,0,0,100.0,2)MAJ(Zippy_Axis_144,MAJ_144,1,Jog_Speed,0,Jog_Accel,0,Jog_Decel,0,0,100.0,100.0,2,1,0,0.0,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="16" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Step 9. Stop 144, reverse 143.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Auto_Running)EQ(Seq_Step,9)MAS(Zippy_Axis_144,MAS_144,0,1,Jog_Decel,0,0,100.0,2)MAJ(Zippy_Axis_143,MAJ_143,1,Jog_Speed,0,Jog_Accel,0,Jog_Decel,0,0,100.0,100.0,2,1,0,0.0,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="17" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Step 10. Stop 143, reverse 142.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Auto_Running)EQ(Seq_Step,10)MAS(Zippy_Axis_143,MAS_143,0,1,Jog_Decel,0,0,100.0,2)MAJ(Zippy_Axis_142,MAJ_142,1,Jog_Speed,0,Jog_Accel,0,Jog_Decel,0,0,100.0,100.0,2,1,0,0.0,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="18" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Step 11. Stop 142, reverse 141. Next DN sends the step to 12 and the wrap rung returns it to 2.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Auto_Running)EQ(Seq_Step,11)MAS(Zippy_Axis_142,MAS_142,0,1,Jog_Decel,0,0,100.0,2)MAJ(Zippy_Axis_141,MAJ_141,1,Jog_Speed,0,Jog_Accel,0,Jog_Decel,0,0,100.0,100.0,2,1,0,0.0,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="19" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Safe default step time, written unconditionally. See the next rung.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOVE(3500,Seq_TMR.PRE);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="20" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Operator value wins only if it is sane. Travel_Time is HMI-writable and feeds the step timer directly; at 0 the TON is done on the scan it starts and all ten motion steps fire in a few milliseconds. Same priority-encoder shape as HMI_Status: safe default written unconditionally above, override here.
GE/LE in series rather than LIM: it is the idiom the rest of this program already uses for a range test, and LIM inverts its own meaning when the low limit exceeds the high one - not a behaviour to leave sitting behind an operator-writable number.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[GE(Travel_Time,500)LE(Travel_Time,10000)MOVE(Travel_Time,Seq_TMR.PRE);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="21" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Step timer for motion steps 2-11. Preset is set by the two rungs above.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Auto_Running)GE(Seq_Step,2)LE(Seq_Step,11)TON(Seq_TMR,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="22" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Shutdown 99. Decel all five to a stop and hold 600 ms on its own timer before dropping servo power.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQ(Seq_Step,99)MAS(Zippy_Axis_141,MAS_141,0,1,Jog_Decel,0,0,100.0,2)MAS(Zippy_Axis_142,MAS_142,0,1,Jog_Decel,0,0,100.0,2)MAS(Zippy_Axis_143,MAS_143,0,1,Jog_Decel,0,0,100.0,2)MAS(Zippy_Axis_144,MAS_144,0,1,Jog_Decel,0,0,100.0,2)MAS(Zippy_Axis_145,MAS_145,0,1,Jog_Decel,0,0,100.0,2)MOVE(600,Stop_TMR.PRE)TON(Stop_TMR,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="23" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Shutdown complete. MSF all five, then return to idle. MSF fires before Seq_Step is cleared.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQ(Seq_Step,99)XIC(Stop_TMR.DN)MSF(Zippy_Axis_141,MSF_141)MSF(Zippy_Axis_142,MSF_142)MSF(Zippy_Axis_143,MSF_143)MSF(Zippy_Axis_144,MSF_144)MSF(Zippy_Axis_145,MSF_145)MOVE(0,Seq_Step)RES(Stop_TMR);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="HMI_Status" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Derives Seq_Status for the FactoryTalk View ME status pill. Read-only view of the sequencer - this routine commands nothing.]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Fault source 1, axis 141. Broken out per axis so the manual screen's summary strip can light the row that is actually faulted instead of a single cell-level lamp that makes the operator go find out which drive it was. The word is latched by the drive until an MAFR, so no seal-in is needed here.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NEQ(Zippy_Axis_141.AxisFault,0)OTE(Axis_Fault_141);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Fault source 1, axis 142. See rung 0.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NEQ(Zippy_Axis_142.AxisFault,0)OTE(Axis_Fault_142);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Fault source 1, axis 143. See rung 0.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NEQ(Zippy_Axis_143.AxisFault,0)OTE(Axis_Fault_143);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Fault source 1, axis 144. See rung 0.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NEQ(Zippy_Axis_144.AxisFault,0)OTE(Axis_Fault_144);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Fault source 1, axis 145. See rung 0.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NEQ(Zippy_Axis_145.AxisFault,0)OTE(Axis_Fault_145);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Roll the five axis lamps into the cell-level summary the status pill reads.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Axis_Fault_141),XIC(Axis_Fault_142),XIC(Axis_Fault_143),XIC(Axis_Fault_144),XIC(Axis_Fault_145)]OTE(Axis_Faulted);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Fault source 2a - the sequencer asked for servo-on and was refused. Broken out per instruction family so the pill and the fault list can say which command was rejected, not just that something was.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(MSO_141.ER),XIC(MSO_142.ER),XIC(MSO_143.ER),XIC(MSO_144.ER),XIC(MSO_145.ER)]OTE(MSO_Error);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Fault source 2b - a jog was refused. This is the one that would otherwise fail silently: the step timer keeps advancing and the conveyor simply never moves.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(MAJ_141.ER),XIC(MAJ_142.ER),XIC(MAJ_143.ER),XIC(MAJ_144.ER),XIC(MAJ_145.ER)]OTE(MAJ_Error);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Fault source 2c - a stop was refused. Treated as a fault, not a nuisance: an axis that will not take a MAS is an axis that will not come down on the shutdown step.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(MAS_141.ER),XIC(MAS_142.ER),XIC(MAS_143.ER),XIC(MAS_144.ER),XIC(MAS_145.ER)]OTE(MAS_Error);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Roll the three command errors into one summary. .ER bits self-clear when the instruction re-executes, so a successful restart clears the pill - there is deliberately no separate acknowledge latch.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(MSO_Error),XIC(MAJ_Error),XIC(MAS_Error)]OTE(Seq_Cmd_Error);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[PRIORITY ENCODER, rungs 10-13. Seq_Status is written unconditionally to STOPPED here and then overwritten in ascending priority below, so the last true rung wins and the tag can never be left stale or undefined on any scan. Read these four rungs as one block; do not reorder them.
0 STOPPED (default) < 1 RUNNING < 2 HOLDING < 3 FAULTED.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOVE(0,Seq_Status);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[1 RUNNING. Auto latched and inside the motion steps 2-11. Step 1 is the MSO settle and is not running yet; step 12 only exists for the single scan before the wrap rung folds it back to 2.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Auto_Running)GE(Seq_Step,2)LE(Seq_Step,11)MOVE(1,Seq_Status);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[2 HOLDING. Commanded transition, motion not at steady state: step 1 is servo-on settling, step 99 is the decel-and-hold before MSF. Step 99 is intentionally NOT gated by Auto_Running - Stop_PB drops that bit on the same scan it forces the shutdown step.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[EQ(Seq_Step,1),EQ(Seq_Step,99)]MOVE(2,Seq_Status);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[3 FAULTED. Highest priority, written last. A drive fault or a refused motion command outranks whatever the step counter thinks it is doing.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Axis_Faulted),XIC(Seq_Cmd_Error),XIC(Servo_On_Timeout)]MOVE(3,Seq_Status);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="14" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[START BLOCKED REASON, this rung and the three below. Same priority-encoder shape as Seq_Status: default written unconditionally, overwritten in ascending priority, last true rung wins. Exists because Manual_Conv unlatches Auto_Running in the same scan AutoSeq_V5 latches it, so a start press in manual does nothing at all and says nothing about why. HMI diagnostic - no rung reads this.
0 clear to start < 3 already running < 2 faulted < 1 in manual.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOVE(0,Start_Blocked_Reason);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="15" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[3 - already running. Lowest priority: true but not the interesting answer.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Auto_Running)MOVE(3,Start_Blocked_Reason);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="16" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[2 - the cell is faulted. Clear the fault before a start will hold.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Axis_Faulted),XIC(Seq_Cmd_Error),XIC(Servo_On_Timeout)]MOVE(2,Start_Blocked_Reason);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="17" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[1 - in manual. Highest priority because it is the one that blocks silently, and the one an operator hits first.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Mode_Manual)MOVE(1,Start_Blocked_Reason);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="MainRoutine" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Auto conveyor sequencer. 0 idle, 1 MSO, 2-6 fwd, 7-11 rev, 99 shutdown. MAJ Dir 0=Fwd 1=Rev.
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[JSR(AutoSeq_V5,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[JSR(Manual_Conv,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[HMI status pill. Runs last so it reports the state the scan actually left the sequencer in, not the state it started in.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[JSR(HMI_Status,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="Manual_Conv" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Manual 141-145 + MAG]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Mode. Manual unlatches Auto_Running so AutoSeq cannot jog a MAG'd follower.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Mode_Manual)OTU(Auto_Running);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Mode_Auto is the inverse lamp.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Mode_Manual)OTE(Mode_Auto);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[141 Enable — MSO while Mode_Manual and Enable_141.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Mode_Manual)XIC(Enable_141)MSO(Zippy_Axis_141,MSO_141);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[141 Running lamp.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Zippy_Axis_141.ServoActionStatus)OTE(Drive_Enabled_141);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[141 Disable — MSF. Release MAG first in class.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Mode_Manual)XIO(Enable_141)MSF(Zippy_Axis_141,MSF_141);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[141 Actuals.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOVE(Zippy_Axis_141.ActualPosition,Act_Pos_141)MOVE(Zippy_Axis_141.ActualVelocity,Act_Vel_141);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[141 START MAM Absolute. Followers blocked while GearingStatus.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Mode_Manual)XIC(Enable_141)XIC(Start_141)ONS(Start_ONS_141)MAM(Zippy_Axis_141,MAM_141,0,Cmd_Pos_141,Cmd_Vel_141,0,Jog_Accel,0,Jog_Decel,0,0,100.0,100.0,2,1,0,0.0,0,0,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[141 STOP MAS All.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Stop_141)MAS(Zippy_Axis_141,MAS_141,0,1,Jog_Decel,0,0,100.0,2);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[141 JOG +10 in/s. Followers blocked while MAG'd.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Mode_Manual)XIC(Enable_141)XIC(Jog_141)MAJ(Zippy_Axis_141,MAJ_141,0,Jog_Speed_Man_141,0,Jog_Accel,0,Jog_Decel,0,0,100.0,100.0,2,1,0,0.0,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[141 JOG release. Gated by Mode_Manual: without it this rung sees the AUTO sequencer's MAJ in process with no manual jog button pressed, and stops it one scan after AutoSeq_V5 starts it - every step, every axis. The jog start rung was already gated; this is the matching undo.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Mode_Manual)XIO(Jog_141)XIC(MAJ_141.IP)MAS(Zippy_Axis_141,MAS_141,1,1,Jog_Decel,0,0,100.0,2);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[141 HOME.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Mode_Manual)XIC(Enable_141)XIC(Home_141)ONS(Home_ONS_141)MAH(Zippy_Axis_141,MAH_141);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[141 RESET MAFR.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Reset_141)ONS(Reset_ONS_141)MAFR(Zippy_Axis_141,MAFR_141);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[142 Enable — MSO while Mode_Manual and Enable_142.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Mode_Manual)XIC(Enable_142)MSO(Zippy_Axis_142,MSO_142);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[142 Running lamp.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Zippy_Axis_142.ServoActionStatus)OTE(Drive_Enabled_142);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="14" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[142 Disable — MSF only if not MAG'd. Un-gear is MAS Gear, not MSF.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Mode_Manual)XIO(Enable_142)XIO(Zippy_Axis_142.GearingStatus)MSF(Zippy_Axis_142,MSF_142);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="15" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[142 Actuals.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOVE(Zippy_Axis_142.ActualPosition,Act_Pos_142)MOVE(Zippy_Axis_142.ActualVelocity,Act_Vel_142);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="16" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[142 START MAM Absolute. Followers blocked while GearingStatus.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Mode_Manual)XIC(Enable_142)XIO(Zippy_Axis_142.GearingStatus)XIC(Start_142)ONS(Start_ONS_142)MAM(Zippy_Axis_142,MAM_142,0,Cmd_Pos_142,Cmd_Vel_142,0,Jog_Accel,0,Jog_Decel,0,0,100.0,100.0,2,1,0,0.0,0,0,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="17" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[142 STOP MAS All.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Stop_142)MAS(Zippy_Axis_142,MAS_142,0,1,Jog_Decel,0,0,100.0,2);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="18" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[142 JOG +10 in/s. Followers blocked while MAG'd.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Mode_Manual)XIC(Enable_142)XIO(Zippy_Axis_142.GearingStatus)XIC(Jog_142)MAJ(Zippy_Axis_142,MAJ_142,0,Jog_Speed_Man_142,0,Jog_Accel,0,Jog_Decel,0,0,100.0,100.0,2,1,0,0.0,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="19" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[142 JOG release. Gated by Mode_Manual: without it this rung sees the AUTO sequencer's MAJ in process with no manual jog button pressed, and stops it one scan after AutoSeq_V5 starts it - every step, every axis. The jog start rung was already gated; this is the matching undo.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Mode_Manual)XIO(Jog_142)XIC(MAJ_142.IP)MAS(Zippy_Axis_142,MAS_142,1,1,Jog_Decel,0,0,100.0,2);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="20" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[142 HOME.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Mode_Manual)XIC(Enable_142)XIO(Zippy_Axis_142.GearingStatus)XIC(Home_142)ONS(Home_ONS_142)MAH(Zippy_Axis_142,MAH_142);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="21" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[142 RESET MAFR.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Reset_142)ONS(Reset_ONS_142)MAFR(Zippy_Axis_142,MAFR_142);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="22" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[143 Enable — MSO while Mode_Manual and Enable_143.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Mode_Manual)XIC(Enable_143)MSO(Zippy_Axis_143,MSO_143);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="23" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[143 Running lamp.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Zippy_Axis_143.ServoActionStatus)OTE(Drive_Enabled_143);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="24" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[143 Disable — MSF only if not MAG'd. Un-gear is MAS Gear, not MSF.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Mode_Manual)XIO(Enable_143)XIO(Zippy_Axis_143.GearingStatus)MSF(Zippy_Axis_143,MSF_143);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="25" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[143 Actuals.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOVE(Zippy_Axis_143.ActualPosition,Act_Pos_143)MOVE(Zippy_Axis_143.ActualVelocity,Act_Vel_143);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="26" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[143 START MAM Absolute. Followers blocked while GearingStatus.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Mode_Manual)XIC(Enable_143)XIO(Zippy_Axis_143.GearingStatus)XIC(Start_143)ONS(Start_ONS_143)MAM(Zippy_Axis_143,MAM_143,0,Cmd_Pos_143,Cmd_Vel_143,0,Jog_Accel,0,Jog_Decel,0,0,100.0,100.0,2,1,0,0.0,0,0,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="27" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[143 STOP MAS All.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Stop_143)MAS(Zippy_Axis_143,MAS_143,0,1,Jog_Decel,0,0,100.0,2);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="28" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[143 JOG +10 in/s. Followers blocked while MAG'd.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Mode_Manual)XIC(Enable_143)XIO(Zippy_Axis_143.GearingStatus)XIC(Jog_143)MAJ(Zippy_Axis_143,MAJ_143,0,Jog_Speed_Man_143,0,Jog_Accel,0,Jog_Decel,0,0,100.0,100.0,2,1,0,0.0,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="29" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[143 JOG release. Gated by Mode_Manual: without it this rung sees the AUTO sequencer's MAJ in process with no manual jog button pressed, and stops it one scan after AutoSeq_V5 starts it - every step, every axis. The jog start rung was already gated; this is the matching undo.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Mode_Manual)XIO(Jog_143)XIC(MAJ_143.IP)MAS(Zippy_Axis_143,MAS_143,1,1,Jog_Decel,0,0,100.0,2);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="30" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[143 HOME.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Mode_Manual)XIC(Enable_143)XIO(Zippy_Axis_143.GearingStatus)XIC(Home_143)ONS(Home_ONS_143)MAH(Zippy_Axis_143,MAH_143);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="31" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[143 RESET MAFR.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Reset_143)ONS(Reset_ONS_143)MAFR(Zippy_Axis_143,MAFR_143);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="32" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[144 Enable — MSO while Mode_Manual and Enable_144.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Mode_Manual)XIC(Enable_144)MSO(Zippy_Axis_144,MSO_144);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="33" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[144 Running lamp.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Zippy_Axis_144.ServoActionStatus)OTE(Drive_Enabled_144);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="34" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[144 Disable — MSF only if not MAG'd. Un-gear is MAS Gear, not MSF.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Mode_Manual)XIO(Enable_144)XIO(Zippy_Axis_144.GearingStatus)MSF(Zippy_Axis_144,MSF_144);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="35" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[144 Actuals.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOVE(Zippy_Axis_144.ActualPosition,Act_Pos_144)MOVE(Zippy_Axis_144.ActualVelocity,Act_Vel_144);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="36" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[144 START MAM Absolute. Followers blocked while GearingStatus.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Mode_Manual)XIC(Enable_144)XIO(Zippy_Axis_144.GearingStatus)XIC(Start_144)ONS(Start_ONS_144)MAM(Zippy_Axis_144,MAM_144,0,Cmd_Pos_144,Cmd_Vel_144,0,Jog_Accel,0,Jog_Decel,0,0,100.0,100.0,2,1,0,0.0,0,0,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="37" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[144 STOP MAS All.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Stop_144)MAS(Zippy_Axis_144,MAS_144,0,1,Jog_Decel,0,0,100.0,2);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="38" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[144 JOG +10 in/s. Followers blocked while MAG'd.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Mode_Manual)XIC(Enable_144)XIO(Zippy_Axis_144.GearingStatus)XIC(Jog_144)MAJ(Zippy_Axis_144,MAJ_144,0,Jog_Speed_Man_144,0,Jog_Accel,0,Jog_Decel,0,0,100.0,100.0,2,1,0,0.0,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="39" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[144 JOG release. Gated by Mode_Manual: without it this rung sees the AUTO sequencer's MAJ in process with no manual jog button pressed, and stops it one scan after AutoSeq_V5 starts it - every step, every axis. The jog start rung was already gated; this is the matching undo.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Mode_Manual)XIO(Jog_144)XIC(MAJ_144.IP)MAS(Zippy_Axis_144,MAS_144,1,1,Jog_Decel,0,0,100.0,2);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="40" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[144 HOME.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Mode_Manual)XIC(Enable_144)XIO(Zippy_Axis_144.GearingStatus)XIC(Home_144)ONS(Home_ONS_144)MAH(Zippy_Axis_144,MAH_144);]]>
</Text>
